{"rows":[{"cols":[{"designInfo":{"stencilSuperIds":["Output"],"stencilId":"cloud-output"},"label":"Configure DataXray Workflows","value":"<p>This admin workflow sets up everything the DataXray sync &amp; search workflows need, in one step. It is <b>idempotent</b> — anything that already exists is left untouched, so it is safe to run again.</p><p><b>It will ensure the following exist (creating them with fixed IDs if missing):</b></p><ul><li>the <b>Collibra to DataXray Integration</b> community</li><li>the <b>DataXray Classifications</b>, <b>DataXray Sync Filter</b> and <b>DataXray Files</b> domains</li><li>the <b>Classification, Annotator, Extractor, Label, DataXray Sync Filter</b> and <b>DataXray File</b> asset types</li><li>the <b>Link, Search Link, Sub Type, DataXray ID, Files, File Path, File Size, Last Modified, Datasource Name, DataXray Datasource ID, DataXray Object ID, DataXray File Name, DataXray Query</b> and <b>Annotated Text Filter</b> attribute types, and assignments so they show on the asset pages</li><li>the <b>returns / returned by</b> relation type linking each search query to the file assets it imported</li></ul><p>On an installation from before the DataXray rename, it also renames these elements and the workflows from their old <b>Data X-Ray</b> names (the queries domain and the <b>Unstructured Data Query</b> asset type both become <b>DataXray Sync Filter</b>). Only elements that still have their old default name are renamed; a name you changed yourself is kept.</p><p>The DataXray workflows (<b>Search</b>, <b>Rerun Search</b>, <b>Sync Classifications</b> and the two <b>Nightly</b> jobs) reference these elements by fixed ID, so once they exist there is nothing further to configure.</p><p><b>You still set the DataXray Base URL and Bearer token by hand</b> on each workflow that calls DataXray — those are their only settings, and this workflow never touches them.</p><p>Click <b>Send</b> to run it. A <b>Configuration Results</b> task will then appear in your task inbox listing what was created, skipped and configured.</p>","defaultValue":false,"size":12,"ignore":false,"visible":true,"enabled":true,"isRequired":false,"id":"startConfigureInfo","type":"htmlComponent"}]}],"metadata":{"key":"startConfigureForm","name":"Configure DataXray Workflows","description":"Confirmation screen shown before the DataXray operating-model bootstrap runs.","version":"1","modelType":"form","flowableDesignVersion":3110,"palette":"flowable-core-form-palette"}}
